# Run 386 evidence archive — only README.md, summary.txt, and .gitignore are tracked.
# Everything else here is preflight/CI-artifact-only or per-run temporary output and MUST NOT be committed.
# In particular NO signature, attestation, or signing-key material is ever committed: the real
# build-provenance attestation is minted only by the disabled-by-default protected workflow
# .github/workflows/public-devnet-release-signing-attestation.yml as a CI artifact, and the generated
# RELEASE_ARTIFACT_MANIFEST.json remains a CI *artifact* (uploaded by
# .github/workflows/public-devnet-release-artifact-manifest.yml), never a committed changing file.
# Node data dirs, node logs, raw /metrics scrape dumps, the staged ci-artifacts/ bundle, the reused
# Run 385 output under run385/, and the generated manifest are temporary and dev/CI-only; only
# publish-safe hashes and status lines appear in the tracked summary/README. The committed, publish-safe
# example manifest lives at docs/release/public-devnet/binary/RELEASE_ARTIFACT_MANIFEST.example.json.
ci-artifacts/
run385/
run384/
node-data/
nodes/
logs/
data/
RELEASE_ARTIFACT_MANIFEST.json
manifest.json
qbind-node.sha256
BUILDID.txt
SIGNING_PREFLIGHT.txt
MANIFEST_VALIDATION_SUMMARY.txt
ATTESTATION_IDENTITY.txt
*.sig
*.sigstore
*.sigstore.json
*.intoto.jsonl
*.dsse
*.attestation
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
clean_metrics.txt
metrics.txt
*.metrics
*.err
*.log
*.metrics.txt
manifest.metrics.txt